% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the customs presumptions. What is taken to be so when a text is silent,
% each rule citing the text that says it: US Customs' publication on apparel
% terminology, and rulings. A derived fact says "according to customs
% presumptions"; the strict reading leaves it out (language reference §14.5,
% §17.5). A stated fact beats a presumed one.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.
    the principal use of *a good* is *a use*.

the templates are:
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a thing* is made of the fabric *a name*; undefined.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*; undefined.
    *a kind* is a kind of knitted garments.
    *a garment* has its construction from a field.
    *a component* is a component of *a good*.
    the fabric of *a garment* is lightweight.
    *a garment* is of plain knit fabric.
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*.
    *a thing* names the material *a name*; undefined.
    *a garment* has an opening starting at the neckline.
    *a garment* is loose-fitting.
    *a value* is a word for babies.
    *a garment* is sized for babies.
    *a name* is a word for rubber.
    *a good* has a coating of plastics.
    *a good* has a coating of rubber.
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for a belt.
    the principal use of *a good* is *a use*.
    *a good* is a set put up for retail sale.

the knowledge base customs presumptions includes these resources:
    materials.

the knowledge base customs presumptions includes:

the apparel terminology publication is published at "https://www.cbp.gov/trade/rulings/informed-compliance-publications".
the text of the apparel terminology publication is at "sources/cbp_icp/apparel_terminology.txt".
ruling NY N361819 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N361819".
the text of ruling NY N361819 is at "sources/cbp/N361819.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 61 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2061".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 61 is at "sources/hts/chapter_61.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 62 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2062".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 62 is at "sources/hts/chapter_62.txt".
the sets publication is published at "https://www.cbp.gov/trade/rulings/informed-compliance-publications".
the text of the sets publication is at "sources/cbp_icp/classification_of_sets.txt".

% A listing offers its parts together, as one product, to the buyer who
% receives it as sold (the listing format: "A listing offers one finished
% product for sale"). The sets publication's third requirement of a set put
% up for retail sale is met; whether the set meets the others is for the
% rules that read it (an ensemble, GRI 3(b) and its essential character).
% A set has "at least two different articles" (requirement (a)): a listing
% that names one part only (a dress with its shawl) is not read as a set.
rule parts_sold_as_one with provenance the sets publication,
        confer "are put up in a manner suitable for sale directly to users without repacking":
a good is a set put up for retail sale
    if a component is a component of the good
    and the kind of the component is a kind
    and an other component is a component of the good
    and the kind of the other component is an other kind
    and the other kind is different from the kind.
the children's apparel publication is published at "https://www.cbp.gov/sites/default/files/assets/documents/2020-Feb/ICP-Childrens-Apparel-2008-Final.pdf".
the text of the children's apparel publication is at "sources/cbp_icp/childrens_apparel.txt".
ruling NY N336251 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N336251".
the text of ruling NY N336251 is at "sources/cbp/N336251.txt".
ruling NY N097520 is published at "https://rulings.cbp.gov/ruling/N097520".
the text of ruling NY N097520 is at "sources/cbp/N097520.txt".

T-shirt is a kind of knitted garments,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "T-shirts (6109, 6111) - are underwear style garments, constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric".
sweater is a kind of knitted garments,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Sweaters (6110, 6111) - are knit garments".
pullover is a kind of knitted garments,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Pullovers (6110, 6111) - are upper body knit garments".
bodysuit is a kind of knitted garments,
    as stated in the apparel terminology publication, confer "Bodysuits and bodyshirts (6114) - are knit one-piece garments".

rule tshirt_fabric with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "T-shirts (6109, 6111) - are underwear style garments, constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric":
the fabric of a garment is lightweight
    if the kind of the garment is T-shirt.

rule tshirt_plain_knit with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or interlock knit fabric":
a garment is of plain knit fabric
    if the kind of the garment is T-shirt.

% A listing's field on how the fabric is made comes first (the marketplace
% listings background reads it); the kind presumes only when it is silent.
rule construction_field_first with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Apparel Terminology under the HTSUS":
a garment has its construction from a field
    if the field "craft of weaving" of the garment reads a value.

% the field of a set speaks of its parts (marketplace listings)
rule construction_field_of_the_set with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "Apparel Terminology under the HTSUS":
a garment has its construction from a field
    if the garment is a component of a good
    and the field "craft of weaving" of the good reads a value.

rule knitted_by_kind with provenance the apparel terminology publication,
        confer "are knit garments":
the fabric construction of a garment is knitted
    if the kind of the garment is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of knitted garments
    and it is not the case that
        the garment has its construction from a field.

rule fleece_knitted with provenance ruling NY N361819,
        confer "polyester knit fleece fabric":
the fabric construction of a garment is knitted
    if the garment is made of the fabric "fleece"
    and it is not the case that
        the garment has its construction from a field.

% Added from the tariff's notes (2026-11-21): what the definition of a kind
% says of a garment that a listing gives that kind.
% Note 4 of Chapters 61 and 62: shirts open at the neckline, blouses are
% loose-fitting
% Not presumed: an opening at the neckline from the word "shirt", nor
% loose-fitting from the word "blouse". Note 4 defines the tariff's shirts
% and blouses, but a shop's "shirt" is often a T-shirt (RatioTariff §3.15).

% Heading 6111 and 6209: a listing for babies is presumed to be of babies'
% garments (note 6(a) of Chapter 61, note 5(a) of Chapter 62: a body height
% not exceeding 86 centimeters)
"baby" is a word for babies,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Babies' garments and clothing accessories, knitted or crocheted".
"babies" is a word for babies,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Babies' garments and clothing accessories, knitted or crocheted".

% Added from US Customs' publication on children's apparel (2026-11-21):
% the names of the babies' size ranges. Left out: "toddler", "toddlers"
% (the publication: "care should be taken not to mistakenly identify items
% for older children, such as toddlers, as babies").
"newborn" is a word for babies,
    as stated in the children's apparel publication, confer "also called newborn sizes".
"newborns" is a word for babies,
    as stated in the children's apparel publication, confer "also called newborn sizes".
"infant" is a word for babies,
    as stated in the children's apparel publication, confer "also called infants' sizes".
"infants" is a word for babies,
    as stated in the children's apparel publication, confer "also called infants' sizes".
"preemie" is a word for babies,
    as stated in the children's apparel publication, confer "range for babies born prematurely".

rule babies_by_gender with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "The expression \"babies' garments and clothing accessories\" means articles for young children of a body height not exceeding 86 centimeters":
a garment is sized for babies
    if the field "gender" of the garment reads a value
    and the value is a word for babies.

% Subheading 6116.10: textile gloves that name a plastic or rubber among
% their materials are presumed to be impregnated, coated, covered or
% laminated with it. A fibre name ("nylon", "acrylic") is not a coating.
"rubber" is a word for rubber,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Impregnated, coated, covered or laminated with plastics or rubber".

rule glove_coating_plastics with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Impregnated, coated, covered or laminated with plastics or rubber":
a good has a coating of plastics
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [gloves, mittens, mitts]
    and the fabric construction of the good is a construction
    and the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for the polymer a polymer
    and it is not the case that
        the name is a word for the textile material a material.

rule glove_coating_rubber with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Impregnated, coated, covered or laminated with plastics or rubber":
a good has a coating of rubber
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [gloves, mittens, mitts]
    and the fabric construction of the good is a construction
    and the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for rubber.

% Added from rulings (2026-11-21): a belt that a listing sells for women,
% men or children girds the waist of the wearer, so it is a clothing
% accessory (3926.20 when it is of plastics). Without a gender the word may
% name a v-belt or a conveyor belt, and nothing is presumed.
"belt" is a word for a belt,
    as stated in ruling NY N336251, confer "The tariff classification of a women’s belt from China".
"belts" is a word for a belt,
    as stated in ruling NY N336251, confer "The tariff classification of a women’s belt from China".

rule belt_worn_by_name with provenance ruling NY N097520,
        confer "The plastic portion of the belt girds the waist and thus constitutes the article known as a belt.":
the principal use of a good is apparel
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for a belt
    and the field "gender" of the good reads a value.

rule belt_worn_by_field with provenance ruling NY N097520,
        confer "The plastic portion of the belt girds the waist and thus constitutes the article known as a belt.":
the principal use of a good is apparel
    if the field "item type" of the good reads a name
    and the name is a word for a belt
    and the field "gender" of the good reads a value.

scenario rulings is:
    the field "item type" of belt one reads "belts".
    the field "gender" of belt one reads "women".
    belt two is called "belt".
    the field "gender" of bodysuit one reads "newborn".
    worn expects answers ["the principal use of belt one is apparel"].
    newborns expects answers ["bodysuit one is sized for babies"].

query worn is:
    the principal use of which good is which use.

query newborns is:
    which garment is sized for babies.

scenario tee is:
    the kind of tee is T-shirt.
    the kind of jumper is sweater.
    the field "craft of weaving" of jumper reads "tat".
    fabrics expects answers ["the fabric of tee is lightweight"].
    constructions expects answers ["the fabric construction of tee is knitted"].
    plain expects answers ["tee is of plain knit fabric"].

scenario tariff_notes is:
    the kind of shirt one is shirt.
    the kind of blouse one is blouse.
    the field "gender" of romper reads "baby".
    the kind of glove is gloves.
    the fabric construction of glove is knitted.
    glove names the material "polyurethane".
    glove names the material "nylon".
    the kind of mitt one is gloves.
    the fabric construction of mitt one is knitted.
    mitt one names the material "rubber".
    openings expects answers [].
    loose expects answers [].
    babies expects answers ["romper is sized for babies"].
    coatings expects answers ["glove has a coating of plastics"].
    rubber coatings expects answers ["mitt one has a coating of rubber"].

query openings is:
    which garment has an opening starting at the neckline.

query loose is:
    which garment is loose-fitting.

query babies is:
    which garment is sized for babies.

query coatings is:
    which good has a coating of plastics.

query rubber coatings is:
    which good has a coating of rubber.

query fabrics is:
    the fabric of which garment is lightweight.

query constructions is:
    the fabric construction of which garment is which construction.

query plain is:
    which garment is of plain knit fabric.

scenario two_piece is:
    top one is a component of outfit one.
    pants one is a component of outfit one.
    the kind of top one is top.
    the kind of pants one is trousers.
    shawl one is a component of gown one.
    the kind of shawl one is shawl.
    retail sets expects answers ["outfit one is a set put up for retail sale"].

query retail sets is:
    which good is a set put up for retail sale.
